An arm notes the core after the one that armed it, which past the last core is none,
and the tick then looks for that core's nearest deadline beyond the cores there are;
a timer line names a core there is.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line comes due before the timer wakes for it
Report: armed timer line names a core there is not

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ void irq_set_bits(struct irq *irq, uint32_t bits)
     }
     /* A timer line wakes the core that armed it, and only that one. */
     if (line_is_timer(irq->line) && bits != 0) {
-        irq->core = (uint8_t)core_index();
+        irq->core = (uint8_t)(core_index() + 1);
         wake_for(irq->deadline);
     }
     irq->bits = bits;
